   "id": "he3",
   "name": "Nutrients and food groups"
  }
 ],
 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Food contains nutrients:\n• carbohydrates: rice, maize, cassava, yams, plantains, bread;\n• proteins: beans, groundnuts, eggs, fish, meat, milk;\n• fats and oils: palm oil, groundnut oil, butter;\n• vitamins: fruits and vegetables such as oranges, mangoes, pawpaw, carrots, huckleberry;\n• minerals: for example calcium (milk, small fish) and iron (liver, green leaves);\n• water and fibre (roughage) are also needed.\nThe three food groups:\n• energy-giving foods: carbohydrates, fats and oils;\n• body-building foods: proteins;\n• protective foods: vitamins and minerals.\nA balanced meal has food from each group, for example rice, beans with fish, and a green vegetable, with fruit after.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "problem": "Is this meal balanced: boiled plantains, fried fish and a mango? If not, what could be added?",
  "steps": [
   "Plantains: energy-giving (carbohydrates). The frying oil is also energy-giving.",
   "Fish: body-building (proteins).",
   "Mango: protective (vitamins).",
   "All three groups are there; a green vegetable would add more minerals."
  ],
  "answer": "Yes, it has all three food groups.",
  "checks": []
 },
